/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.DS_Store

# Read-only reference checkouts (1.9 GB of gpui-component and friends). They are
# other people's repositories, cloned for reading — never edited, never imported,
# and reproducible with a clone. See CLAUDE.md.
/.research/

# Release scaffolding output.
/dist/

# Planning material — the product review, the roadmap, the per-screen specs and
# the decisions ledger. Kept on disk because the work still leans on it, out of
# the repository because it is a private workbench: what a contributor needs is
# in README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md, and what is still open belongs in issues.
/docs/

# The imported design mockup that the first pass was built from. It did its
# job; the application is the reference now. Kept on disk, and available to
# anyone who wants to redesign the thing — just not carried by the repository.
/.design/

# Working agents for this codebase, which are notes to one maintainer rather
# than something a contributor needs. The release manager is the exception: it
# is the release procedure written down in a form that can be run.
/.claude/agents/*
!/.claude/agents/release-manager.md
!/.claude/agents/dependency-warden.md
!/.claude/agents/import-forensics.md

# Scratch space for demo material — a sample vault, capture scripts, whatever
# a screenshot needed that day. Useful locally, not part of the product.
/tools/
